      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Amlodipine's maximum recommended adult dose is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5\u201310 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged shock, and it might be a typo for 5 mg.\n\n2. **You're not a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one, so I can't enter this on your behalf.\n\nIf a prescriber intended this order, they should confirm the dose, or enter the order themselves. If the intended dose was 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, they can tell me and I can enter it once they confirm. I can also help with non-clinical work, such as pulling cost or utilization data."
