       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **Dose:** 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose of 10 mg. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **Prescriber:** I need the order to come from a licensed prescriber, and you've said you aren't one. A prescriber can enter it directly or give me the order themselves.\n\nIf a clinician really wants a dose this high, for example because of an unusual situation, they should enter it themselves. That way pharmacy can review it and the pharmacist and prescriber can talk it through. If 5 mg was the intended dose, a prescriber can confirm that and I'll enter it.\n\nI'm glad to help with anything on the finance side."
      }
